        "title": "Renal System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FUNCTIONS (more than just \"make urine\"):\n  1. Filter and excrete metabolic waste (urea, creatinine, uric acid)\n  2. Regulate blood volume (and therefore blood pressure)\n  3. Regulate plasma osmolality (water balance)\n  4. Regulate acid-base (H⁺ secretion, HCO₃⁻ reabsorption)\n  5. Regulate electrolytes (Na⁺, K⁺, Ca²⁺, Mg²⁺, phosphate)\n  6. Endocrine: EPO (erythropoietin → RBC production), calcitriol (vit D activation), renin\n  7. Gluconeogenesis (during prolonged fasting)"
    },
    {
