      },
      "text": "```\nNEPHRON ANATOMY:\n  Glomerulus + Bowman's capsule (filtration)\n       ↓\n  Proximal convoluted tubule — PCT (bulk reabsorption)\n       ↓\n  Loop of Henle:\n    Descending limb (thin, water-permeable) → Hairpin turn\n    Ascending limb (thick, impermeable to water, ion-pumping)\n       ↓\n  Distal convoluted tubule — DCT (fine-tuning; hormone-sensitive)\n       ↓\n  Collecting duct (CD) — hormone-sensitive water permeability (ADH)\n       ↓\n  Medullary collecting duct → papilla → minor calyx → urine\n```"
    },
